;; Samples for the github-linguist submission.
;;
;; Provenance, not copies. Linguist wants real-world sources committed into its
;; own `samples/Kotoba/` directory, and a frozen duplicate kept here would be
;; one more vendored copy aging on its own schedule -- the failure this repo
;; family already knows by name. Each entry names the repo, path and commit to
;; fetch from at submission time:
;;
;;   git -C <checkout> show <commit>:<path> > samples/Kotoba/<as>
;;
;; All four are Apache-2.0 and are production sources, not tutorial code --
;; CONTRIBUTING.md: "'Hello world' and other examples found in tutorials will
;; not be accepted." State the licence in the PR body.

